  "editor": {
    "comment": "Role vocabulary for code editors and note-takers. One name space, rendered into Zed, VS Code, Obsidian and Logseq. Syntax is achromatic on purpose: category is carried by luminance step plus slope and weight, never by hue. The accent appears here only where rule 1 already allows it, on links, the caret, selection and the active item. depth-1 to depth-6 is a single ordinal ladder, reused wherever a host wants six distinguishable slots for something that is really a depth or a rank: bracket nesting, heading level, chart series. Renderers read it monotonically for headings and charts and in an alternating order for brackets, where adjacent levels must separate. Every role must exist in both light and dark; build.mjs rejects a role defined in only one.",

    "style": {
      "comment": "Slope and weight, applied identically in both modes. These do half the work hue would otherwise do.",
      "syn-keyword": "bold",
      "syn-tag": "bold",
      "syn-title": "bold",
      "syn-strong": "bold",
      "syn-invalid": "bold",
      "syn-type": "italic",
